      "license": "MIT",
      "notes": [
        "Private sections.sign-in-form renderer composes public Form, ContentSection, TextField and Button. There is no public sign-in Block export.",
        "Mapping identifies Form adaptation regions, not type-equivalent SignInForm props. Header.heading is rendered by the surrounding ContentSection heading and aria-labelledby on Form; providers, credential fields and verification fields are composed children.",
        "Provider labels and every input/action/error string are host-authored passage content. Sensitive controlled values never enter runtime JSON content. Existing ConsumerRuntimePorts.sectionHosts carries phase, values, pending, onValueChange and onSubmit, plus onProvider/onBack/onResend for visible actions.",
        "Credentials and code are bounded host-selected UI phases only. Provider actions delegate ids; form submission delegates the current phase. No authentication, auth-provider import, redirect, session check, completed state, account creation, invitation, or reset behavior is claimed.",
        "Without a Section host the sample renders disabled controls. Pending blocks repeated submission and value changes. The host performs validation and authenticates; errors remain host-supplied copy.",
        "Descriptor only; package fill coverage does not prove consumer runtime conformance.",
        "Source-only import and token-read measurements are lower bounds; shared anatomy, accessibility, contrast and consumer runtime conformance remain unmeasured. Content bindings describe host adaptation points, not type-equivalent converters."
      ],
